  "description": "With one source the model has rank 0 and the weight is fixed at 1 by construction, so the only thing being tested is whether target and source form a clade relative to the outgroups. Comparing this with the two-source fit shows why a weight vector on its own says nothing: the weight here is 100% regardless of how badly the model fits.",
  "caveats": [
    "Computed from admixtools::example_f2_blocks, the f2-statistics bundled with ADMIXTOOLS 2 for seven populations (Altai Neanderthal, Vindija, Denisova, Mbuti, Chimp, Russia_Ust_Ishim, Switzerland_Bichon). These are real data and the statistics are genuine, but they are the package's demonstration populations -- archaic hominins and Palaeolithic modern humans. This is NOT a South Asian analysis and must not be presented as one. South Asian examples require the AADR reference panel built by data/pipeline/.",
    "qpAdm does not identify the true history. A model that is not rejected is consistent with these data given this outgroup set; other untested models may fit as well or better. p-values depend on the right populations, the SNP set and the jackknife block size."
  ],
